1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,309
In this lesson, we'll look after your
customers' data and their choices: who you're

2
00:00:05,309 --> 00:00:10,060
allowed to contact, how opt-outs work, and
what to do when someone asks for a copy

3
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:10,871
of their data.

4
00:00:11,722 --> 00:00:16,314
Privacy laws like GDPR in the UK
and Europe, and the TCPA in the US,

5
00:00:16,314 --> 00:00:20,299
say you need permission before
you send marketing messages.

6
00:00:20,299 --> 00:00:23,946
Carriers and inbox providers
watch for complaints too.

7
00:00:23,946 --> 00:00:28,066
Kyntlo gives you the tools to
stay on the right side of both.

8
00:00:28,066 --> 00:00:31,713
Rules differ by country, so
check what applies to you.

9
00:00:32,564 --> 00:00:35,885
Open a contact, and
scroll to Do Not Disturb.

10
00:00:35,885 --> 00:00:40,903
DND stops Kyntlo sending on a
channel: emails, text messages, calls,

11
00:00:40,903 --> 00:00:42,232
WhatsApp and more.

12
00:00:42,232 --> 00:00:46,881
Olivia has asked for no more
texts, so switch on Text messages.

13
00:00:46,881 --> 00:00:49,833
Her emails and calls carry on as normal.

14
00:00:50,683 --> 00:00:55,206
DND all channels blocks every
outgoing message in one switch.

15
00:00:55,206 --> 00:01:00,766
And Inbound calls & SMS blocks their
replies too, which is useful for spam.

16
00:01:00,766 --> 00:01:04,325
DND also overrides your
workflows and campaigns,

17
00:01:04,325 --> 00:01:08,180
so a contact who opted out
is skipped automatically.

18
00:01:09,031 --> 00:01:12,888
Most of the time, you won't
need to switch this yourself.

19
00:01:12,888 --> 00:01:17,691
When someone replies STOP to a text,
Kyntlo turns on text DND for them.

20
00:01:17,691 --> 00:01:21,751
When they click unsubscribe in
an email, email DND turns on.

21
00:01:21,751 --> 00:01:26,284
Never switch these back on unless
the customer clearly asks you to.

22
00:01:27,135 --> 00:01:30,724
It also helps to record when
someone gave you permission.

23
00:01:30,724 --> 00:01:34,816
In Settings, Custom Fields, click
Add Field, and choose Checkbox.

24
00:01:35,665 --> 00:01:39,046
Name it Marketing consent,
put it in a Consent folder,

25
00:01:39,046 --> 00:01:41,801
and write the exact
wording people agree to.

26
00:01:41,801 --> 00:01:44,243
Add this field to your forms, unticked,

27
00:01:44,243 --> 00:01:47,499
so every new lead's choice
is saved on their record.

28
00:01:48,349 --> 00:01:52,840
Sometimes a customer asks for a copy
of the data you hold about them.

29
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:55,964
In Contacts, tick their
name, and choose Export.

30
00:01:55,964 --> 00:01:58,567
You'll get a CSV file you can send them.

31
00:01:59,419 --> 00:02:03,287
If someone asks you to delete
their data, delete the contact.

32
00:02:03,287 --> 00:02:07,979
Deleted contacts stay in the Restore
tab for a while, in case of mistakes,

33
00:02:07,979 --> 00:02:11,530
so you can bring one back if
it was removed by accident.

34
00:02:12,380 --> 00:02:16,803
Finally, Audit Logs in Settings
shows who changed what, and when.

35
00:02:16,803 --> 00:02:20,681
Here's Sarah turning on text
DND for Olivia this morning.

36
00:02:20,681 --> 00:02:25,580
If a customer ever asks how their
data was handled, this is your record.

37
00:02:26,429 --> 00:02:30,620
And remember lesson 1.5: only
give the Bulk Actions permission,

38
00:02:30,620 --> 00:02:34,545
which includes exporting, to
the people who really need it.

39
00:02:34,545 --> 00:02:39,136
The fewer people who can download
your contact list, the safer it is.

40
00:02:39,985 --> 00:02:40,998
Here's a pro tip.

41
00:02:40,998 --> 00:02:44,929
Never import a list of people who
haven't agreed to hear from you,

42
00:02:44,929 --> 00:02:46,239
even if you bought it.

43
00:02:46,239 --> 00:02:51,004
Complaints from one bad list can get your
number blocked and your emails sent to

44
00:02:51,004 --> 00:02:52,076
spam for everyone.

45
00:02:52,927 --> 00:02:56,480
That's Module 14 done, and
your account is fully set up!

46
00:02:56,480 --> 00:03:01,555
In Module 15, we'll put everything together
and build a complete lead-to-booking

47
00:03:01,555 --> 00:03:03,078
system, start to finish.

48
00:03:03,078 --> 00:03:03,966
See you there.
